00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:05.030 align:start position:0%
more signs of america's support for  ukraine on only his second visit to the  war zone since the conflict began more  than six months ago u.s secretary of  state anthony blinken made an  unannounced trip to key  blinken announced two billion dollars in  military assistance to ukraine and 18  countries in the region to counter what  he called russian aggression  also on thursday u.s defense secretary  lloyd austin in a visit to germany  announced a new  675 million dollar aid package for  ukraine  the pledges come as ukraine seems to  have gained momentum on the battlefield  at least in the north east where an  offensive against russian positions in  harkev region have shown early signs of  success  ukrainian forces say they have retaken  some 20 villages and towns and pushed  more than 50 kilometers past the front  lines into russian hill territory  videos from the front line seem to show  their units moving forward advancing on  russian entrenched positions  harkiev is the second largest city in  ukraine since the beginning of the war  it's remained firmly in ukrainian hands  however for months russia has controlled  much of the area to the east and south  the ukrainian advance appears to be  retaking all of harkiev to better  reinforce the defenses in the regional  capital  the ukrainians have clearly seized the  momentum in this war both with the visit  by america's top diplomat here to the  capitol with promises of more aid as  well as momentum on the battlefield with  clear territorial gains in the northeast  but this is also a war where momentum  can change quickly  gabriel zondo al jazeera keefe
 

